    "referenceImplementation": "OpenSSL",
    "referenceImplementationNote": "OpenSSL is used as the single reference implementation for every entry, because it is the most widely deployed open TLS/crypto library and every one of its stable releases is dated by a GitHub tag. Using one library keeps the lag comparable across primitives; a different library (BoringSSL, libsodium, rustls) sometimes shipped a primitive earlier, so these lags are an upper bound on 'first open implementation anywhere'.",
    "curationNote": "Curated and human-reviewable. Every entry cites both the standard and the exact implementing release. Dates given at month precision use the first of the month; the lag is a years-scale quantity so day precision does not matter. Extend this file (do not scrape at build time) to densify the series.",
